import{_ as t,o as a,c as o,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-046 — The launch runs a seeded camera director; its light comes from the real launch time","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-046-the-launch-runs-a-seeded-camera-director.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-046-the-launch-runs-a-seeded-camera-director.md"}'),n={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-046-the-launch-runs-a-seeded-camera-director.md"};function i(d,e,r,l,c,h){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="uxd-046-—-the-launch-runs-a-seeded-camera-director-its-light-comes-from-the-real-launch-time" tabindex="-1">UXD-046 — The launch runs a seeded camera director; its light comes from the real launch time <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-046-—-the-launch-runs-a-seeded-camera-director-its-light-comes-from-the-real-launch-time" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-046 — The launch runs a seeded camera director; its light comes from the real launch time&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted (built; unit and e2e tests green, see Verification)</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-15</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-15 — &quot;It is all fucking amazing&quot; (the director prototype clips), then &quot;1 yes&quot; to wiring it into /fly, and &quot;Real missions should take their lighting from the actual launch time in local time, and we seed on /fly after Plan when the user makes his own launches.&quot;</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: LA1 (camera on top, moving around), LA1a-d, FY2 (the first seconds rise vertically), D6 (example shots)</li><li><strong>Builds on</strong>: <a href="./UXD-042-plan-to-fly-handoff-grouped-destinations-and-the-journey-bar">UXD-042</a> (the play bar and its marker row stay as they are), RFC-034 (the launch act)</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/orbital/ascent-director.ts</code>, <code>launch-sun.ts</code>, <code>launch-director-debug-plot.ts</code>, <code>src/lib/launches/launch-instant.ts</code>, <code>src/lib/three/launch-director-rig.ts</code>, <code>launch-conditions-scene.ts</code>, <code>LaunchScene.svelte</code>, <code>/fly</code> <code>+page.svelte</code>, <code>/dev/launch-director</code></li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The launch camera was nine fixed side views: after T+22 s one <code>chase</code> shot could play for minutes, every launch looked the same, the climb slid sideways (the pad&#39;s 0.41 km/s counted as downrange) and the body leaned while its base was still beside the tower. The sky was a flat blue gradient with no clouds, smoke or light variety.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>The director is the default camera on /fly&#39;s launch.</strong> A seeded shot plan per launch (the vehicle id and the mission id: the same launch always replays the same, different launches differ), an opening drawn from a pool (today&#39;s long-lens <code>tower_clear</code>, a pad-level wide, an overhead drop, a dusk wide), shot pools by altitude band, a beat for Max-Q, each separation and the fairing, eased blends of 1.3 s of screen time, hard cuts on the beats, the framing solved so the vehicle fills 40 to 70 % of the frame height (the one <code>wide_trail</code> per launch excepted). The plan is built once at a fixed authoring speed, so a speed change never reshuffles shots, and it is a pure function of the mission time: scrubbing, seeking and pausing never jump.</li><li><strong>The first seconds are a vertical rise.</strong> The scene draws the ground-relative path (the pad&#39;s rotation speed subtracted) and keeps the body upright until its base is above the tower, then blends (quintic) to the ground-relative flight path. The physics, the HUD and the play bar stay inertial.</li><li><strong>Conditions.</strong> A light pick (midday, golden, dusk, night), a cloud cover (clear, scattered, deck, heavy) with stratus and cumulus, a limb glow coloured by the light, pad smoke that rolls out sideways and is lit by the plume, a lattice tower, city lights on the night side, a plume light on the stack. All procedural (shader noise, canvas sprites); no new asset or dependency.</li><li><strong>The light comes from the real launch time when it is known.</strong> The Sun at the pad (the mission&#39;s launch-site fleet ref, else the launches entry&#39;s pad, else the profile&#39;s site) at the launch instant from <code>launches-historic</code> sets the light and the sun&#39;s direction: night below -6 degrees, dusk -6 to +6 (dawn included), golden +6 to +15, midday above. A Plan flight (<code>plan-…</code> id), a mission with a date but no time of day, or one with no entry is <strong>seeded</strong>, never given an invented noon. A <code>?light=</code> on the dev route still wins. Clouds and smoke stay seeded.</li><li><strong>The Shuttle&#39;s payload stays in the bay.</strong> Galileo, Magellan and Ulysses have no injection or separation beat and no deployment (<code>payloadInBay</code>); the Shuttle&#39;s launch times match NASA&#39;s STS-30, STS-34 and STS-41 pages.</li><li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>: the plan has hard cuts only and each shot holds its midpoint pose (no sweeping moves, no blends, no wobble).</li><li><strong>A/B for one release.</strong> <code>?cam=classic</code> keeps today&#39;s camera and scene. <code>data-camera-mode</code> and <code>data-director-shot</code> on the launch scene name the mode and the active shot.</li><li><strong><code>?debug=1</code></strong> adds the launch-director view to /fly&#39;s DebugPanel (the ascent path, every planned shot&#39;s camera and look direction, the live camera and trail, a readout).</li><li>Weak GPUs and touch devices get a lighter conditions rig (fewer sphere segments and smoke puffs).</li></ol><h2 id="not-done-here" tabindex="-1">Not done here <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-done-here" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Not done here&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Frame time on a real phone or GPU (measured only under software GL).</li><li>A free-look nudge (drag) with a hand-back, a keyboard route.</li><li>Real launch azimuth for the sun (downrange is taken as east).</li><li>Real times for missions the launches dataset has no entry for (about 75 % of the missions are seeded).</li></ul><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>ascent-director.test.ts</code>, <code>launch-sun.test.ts</code>, <code>launch-instant.test.ts</code>, <code>launch-director-rig.test.ts</code>, <code>payload-in-bay.test.ts</code> (see the commit); <code>tests/e2e/fly-launch.spec.ts</code> on desktop and mobile Chromium: the director by default, <code>?cam=classic</code> the old camera, the existing launch tests unchanged.</p>',10)])])}const g=t(n,[["render",i]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
